  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9bc4902ccea98cf44865aecb61fc1ff4, type: 3}
  m_Name: Ivan
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SuspectData
  FirstName: Ivan
  LastName: Tarkov
  Nickname: The Serial Killer
  Occupation: Factory Worker
  CharacterDescription: Friendly, upbeat, constant smile that never drops, eyes feel
    empty. Clearly hiding something but not really trying to hide it that well, almost
    like he wants you to notice he's a serial killer in secret. Maniacal, creepy
    grin and soulless eyes.
  CharacterArc: Maniacal grin, empty white eyes, and a terrifyingly upbeat attitude.
    His arc is about predatory glee. As society collapses, he stops hiding his nature
    entirely, viewing the apocalypse as a playground where the rules of man no longer
    apply.
  DateOfBirth: 18/04/1954
  Sex: Male
  EntryPermitExpiryDate: 19 NOV
  IsResident: 1
  GivesPaperwork: 1
  handwritingFont: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f8e89ead54f8523428cc2e34f005bb5e, type: 2}
  startingInfectionScore: 0
  dailyInfectionProgression: 5
  IDPhoto: {fileID: 2800000, guid: c0072b0f37423214fad965cf6682ff95, type: 3}
  CharacterPrefab: {fileID: 7584919870796122196, guid: 3ab329df9f896a74294f492fa0087291, type: 3}
  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning to residential block after the late shift.
    - Resident returning to the industrial district.
    - Picking up a new pair of industrial work boots.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Escaping the rising radiation levels in the sector.
    - Checking on the status of the factory power grid.
    - Seeking shelter from the toxic rainfall.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Returning to assigned bunk for the final curfew.
    - Seeking refuge from the heavy black ash.
    - Fulfilling mandatory residency check-in.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Picking up a paycheck from a factory that closed in 1982.
    - Shopping for jewelry at the hardware store.
    - Visiting a friend who disappeared three years ago.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Returning to a house that was turned into a crater.
    - Buying a shovel to bury a very heavy secret.
    - Meeting a coworker in the middle of a minefield.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Going home to count the collection in my cellar.
    - To see if the neighbors have stopped screaming yet.
    - I need to find out what color the inside of a ghost is.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Beautiful day for a walk, isn't it? I feel absolutely wonderful!
    - Just heading back from the factory. Hard work makes for a happy heart.
    - Why the long face, officer? You should try smiling more. Like me!
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "Have you noticed how quiet the alleys are getting? It\u2019s perfect for...
      hobbies."
    - "I found a new tool today. It\u2019s heavy, balanced, and very, very sharp."
    - "Don't look at my eyes. Look at my teeth. They\u2019re much more interesting."
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - The world is finally matching the inside of my head. I love it!
    - Can you hear the music? It sounds like everyone screaming at once.
    - "I\u2019m going home to play. There are so many toys left in the dark."
  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - "See you tomorrow! I\u2019ll bring you something special. Maybe."
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Keep that neck straight, officer. Desk work is awful for your posture.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Thanks, comrade. Keep out of trouble now!
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Oh, a private room? How thoughtful of you!
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I hope you have strong locks. For your sake, not mine.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "You\u2019re just putting me in a box with more toys. Thank you!"
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Oh! What a surprise! I didn't think you had it in you!
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "Look at all that red! It\u2019s even prettier than I imagined!"
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Finally... the big... bright... joke... is over.
  voiceAudioClips: []
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The factory! Long shift, but a great one. Very productive.
    midDaysAnswer: Oh, here and there. A few errands. Nothing you'd find interesting.
      Probably.
    finalDaysAnswer: Everywhere! The city is so quiet now. So many empty places to
      explore!
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Me? No, no, no. I feel absolutely wonderful. Better than ever,
      actually!
    midDaysAnswer: My eyes have been a little dry. It makes it hard to blink. But
      I try not to anyway!
    finalDaysAnswer: I've never felt more myself. That's not a symptom, is it?
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Just me! I prefer it that way. More room for my hobbies.
    midDaysAnswer: Just me now. My last roommate... moved away. Suddenly.
    finalDaysAnswer: No one anymore! The apartment is very tidy these days.
  IDNumber: 1893438
